---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro'
import Emblem from '../components/Emblem.astro'
---
<BaseLayout
  title="Dao De Deseret Foundation"
  appendSiteName={false}
  active="home"
  mainClass="page page-home"
>
  <section class="temple-hero">
    <Emblem />
    <p class="eyebrow">Comparative theology · philosophy · disciplined reflection</p>
    <h1>Dao De Deseret Foundation</h1>
    <nav class="sancai-frieze" aria-label="The three paths">
      <a href="/dao" title="Dao · Heaven">天</a>
      <span class="sep" aria-hidden="true">·</span>
      <a href="/de" title="De · Human">人</a>
      <span class="sep" aria-hidden="true">·</span>
      <a href="/deseret" title="Deseret · Earth">地</a>
    </nav>
    <p class="lede lede-strong">
      A foundation for comparative theology, philosophical study, and disciplined
      religious reflection, organized around three paths of approach—<em>Dao</em>,
      <em>De</em>, and <em>Deseret</em>. Its gathering body is the
      <a class="inline-link" href="/lodge">Lodge of Deseret</a>.
    </p>
    <div class="ornament short"><span class="lozenge">❖</span></div>
  </section>

  <section class="statement-block">
    <p class="illuminated">
      Some differences between traditions are irreducible. Others are differences of
      emphasis, symbol, sequence, or speech. The task here is not to flatten them into
      sameness, but to place them near enough to one another that their convergences,
      frictions, and residues can actually be seen, heard, experienced, and integrated.
      Where they do converge, it is often by <em>metaphorical isomorphism</em>—the same
      underlying structure carried in different images, one tradition's metaphor mapping,
      point for point, onto another's.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="home-grid home-grid-tight">
    <article class="card ink-card">
      <h2>Orientation</h2>
      <p>
        The Foundation exists for careful comparison, study, and mutual correction. It
        assumes that seriousness requires both learning and revision, and that a person
        can be faithful to the best of a tradition without being imprisoned by its most
        anxious forms. Its charge is the old one: to establish <em>a house of learning…
        a house of order, a house of God</em>.
      </p>
    </article>

    <article class="card ink-card">
      <h2>The Three Paths</h2>
      <div class="path-stack">
        <div class="path-line">
          <strong>Dao — The Way</strong>
          <span>Heaven · 天 — practice, movement, alignment</span>
        </div>
        <div class="path-line">
          <strong>De — The Witness</strong>
          <span>Human · 人 — lived experience, first-person disclosure</span>
        </div>
        <div class="path-line">
          <strong>Deseret — The Order</strong>
          <span>Earth · 地 — covenant, law, memory, sacred form</span>
        </div>
      </div>
      <p><a href="/library" class="inline-link">Library &amp; Reading Paths</a></p>
    </article>

    <article class="card ink-card">
      <h2>Lodge of Deseret</h2>
      <p>
        The Lodge is the Foundation's gathering body—its recurring forum for study
        sessions, round-tables, and recorded proceedings. Its founding chapter,
        <strong>The Holy Smoke</strong>, is the living hearth where it convenes.
      </p>
      <p><a href="/lodge" class="inline-link">The Lodge &amp; its Register</a></p>
    </article>
  </section>

  <section class="note-block framed-note ink-frame">
    <h2>Sister Bodies</h2>
    <p>
      The work is carried by two sister bodies. The <strong>Dao De Deseret Foundation</strong>
      keeps the Library and convenes the Lodge, so study can become fellowship.
      The <strong>Dao De Deseret Research Institute</strong> carries that study into
      scholarship and publishes
      <a class="inline-link" href="https://valencejournal.com" rel="noopener">Valence Journal</a>.
    </p>
  </section>

  <div class="ornament"><span class="lozenge">❖</span></div>

  <section class="note-block framed-note ink-frame">
    <h2>How the work is entered</h2>
    <p>
      The Foundation is approached in degrees—concentric, not hierarchical. One may remain
      at any ring; each contains the whole.
    </p>
    <ul class="degrees">
      <li>
        <span class="degree-name">Reader</span>
        <span class="degree-gloss">Anyone who walks the three paths through the Library. The door is open and unguarded.</span>
      </li>
      <li>
        <span class="degree-name">Lodge of Deseret</span>
        <span class="degree-gloss">Those who gather to study together, and whose conversation is kept as a register.</span>
      </li>
      <li>
        <span class="degree-name">The Holy Smoke</span>
        <span class="degree-gloss">The founding chapter—the hearth that actually convenes the Lodge.</span>
      </li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section class="note-block framed-note ink-frame">
    <h2>Working Principle</h2>
    <p>
      A house of study should not exist to preserve the certainty of its members. It
      should exist to refine awareness, enlarge patience, and make revision less
      frightening than self-protection.
    </p>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
